# Reflection
The screen has identified 31 hits with strong effects on IFNG production. Analysis reveals two major regulatory pathways: (1) negative regulators including ZAP70, VAV1, TRAF6, JAK1, and LCK that suppress IFNG when perturbed, and (2) positive regulators like TSC1 and NFKB2 that enhance IFNG. The hits are enriched in TCR signaling, NF-κB pathway components, and JAK-STAT signaling. Given the strong negative effects from lymphocyte-specific kinases (ZAP70, LCK, JAK1) and adaptor proteins (VAV1, TRAF6), the next round should prioritize: upstream TCR components, additional JAK-STAT pathway members, NF-κB regulators, and epigenetic modifiers that showed promise (KDM1A, KMT2A).

# Research Plan
